<%# Footer: the placeholder mailto (metadata.email was a literal
    your-email@example.com stub) is gone - no personal contact info belongs
    in a public build. In its place: a link to the public GitHub repo (for
    source/contributing), a link to /credits/ (Andy Andrea as
    idea originator, the archivists/mirrors, and GitHub contributors), and
    the content license line. The site is a content surface, so only the
    written content's CC BY 4.0 license is shown here (the short brand-form
    attribution string); the source code's separate MIT license is a repo
    concern (LICENSE) and is intentionally not surfaced on the site. Mirrors
    the `license` asserted in the JSON-LD graph (src/_components/json_ld.rb)
    and the rel=license link in _head.erb. %>
<footer class="site-footer">
  <%= render "flourish" %>
  <p class="site-footer__line">
    <a href="<%= metadata.repo_url %>">GitHub</a>
    &middot;
    <a href="/credits/">Credits</a>
  </p>
  <p class="site-footer__line site-footer__license">
    Ruby Lore (chunkybacon.dev), <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" rel="license">CC BY 4.0</a>
  </p>
</footer>
